The message of an unresolved identifier is chosen when its lookup fails

getResolvedSymbol and resolveEntityName chose the "cannot find name" message before the lookup:
getCannotFindNameDiagnosticForName compares the identifier's text with some forty names, for
every identifier a check resolves, and nearly every lookup finds its name. A lookup that starts
at the identifier itself now passes cannotFindNameOfLocation, and onFailedToResolveSymbol asks
for the message with the location it was given, which is that identifier. A lookup from another
location (resolveEntityName with a location) chooses the message first, as before.

